    "created_at": "2025-12-07T04:30:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-07T04:30:54Z",
    "body": "The existing Minecraft server status widget does need to be changed, imo. Having the server's logo doesn't add much value to the widget; I don't think that most people spinning up a Minecraft server usually set a server logo, so the widget ends up rendering a generic square (and before it rendered nothing at all if no logo was present). \n\nWhen a friend asked me to change the status widget icon for his server to a grass block instead of the generic square, he was shocked to learn that I couldn't do it, and was unaware that he could set a Minecraft server logo when I told him that *he* had to set it. It'd be more handy to be able to set an icon for the widget within Homarr.\n\nBut, that aside, my main reason for requesting a Gamedig powered generic server status widget is for every other game server. It would be nice to also have status widgets for my other game servers (Valhiem, Terraria, Vintage Story, plus a few more) for myself and my friends to see the status of each server and who is playing.\n\nInstead of needing to maintain and update a bunch of game server status widgets, I think it makes a lot of sense to have a generic widget powered by the Gamedig library, which would cover *every* game server. A standard query response object is returned for each game server query, so I'd imagine it'd be mostly a matter of designing a generic UI to represent the all data returned plus the title of the game. \n\nI'd personally be okay with the loss of the Minecraft server icon. I'd rather have a status widget that looks nice, handles more games, and displays as much data as it can rather than have an icon pulled from the server.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
